WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.735
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Sunday, October twenty fifth.

2
00:00:04.735 --> 00:00:12.307
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.307 --> 00:00:15.533
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:17.434
We start in the Middle East.

5
00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:26.392
On Friday, the State Department updated its travel advisories across the region to reflect the threat of increased Iranian supported Houthi regional aggression.

6
00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.792
The advisory levels did not change.

7
00:00:28.792 --> 00:00:36.727
Saudi Arabia remains at Level Three, Reconsider Travel, and notices for Iraq, Israel, Lebanon and the United Arab Emirates were also updated.

8
00:00:36.727 --> 00:00:52.172
On Iran, the Institute for the Study of War and the Critical Threats Project report that on Friday, the Director of National Intelligence warned that US intelligence assessments indicate Iran is in the advanced stages of planning attacks against US targets in the region.

9
00:00:52.172 --> 00:00:59.825
And Reuters reports, citing the Tasnim news agency, that Iran's army says it shot down a US drone over Bandar Abbas today.

10
00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:10.842
In Yemen, Deccan Chronicle reports the Houthis claimed an attack on a naval base and the Al Nasr military camp in Aden, the seat of the internationally recognized government, after blasts were heard in the city.

11
00:01:10.842 --> 00:01:13.263
No casualty figures have been reported.

12
00:01:13.263 --> 00:01:21.416
Separately, on Thursday, October twenty second, al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula attacked government aligned forces in Shabwah province.

13
00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:29.825
The Kuwait News Agency reports two soldiers were killed, and the outlet South twenty four reports two killed and six wounded.

14
00:01:29.825 --> 00:01:42.410
In Ukraine, Hromadske Radio reports that on Thursday, October twenty second, regional authorities expanded the mandatory evacuation of families with children to every settlement in the Kramatorsk and Sloviansk communities in Donetsk region.

15
00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:48.650
Radio Free Europe reports evacuations from Kramatorsk are accelerating as Russian attacks intensify.

16
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:57.388
Inside Russia, Reuters reports a drone attack injured five people and damaged an industrial facility in the Perm region, according to the governor.

17
00:01:57.388 --> 00:02:04.526
In Japan, the US Geological Survey reported a magnitude seven point zero earthquake in the Bonin Islands region.

18
00:02:04.526 --> 00:02:07.193
No damage reports have been seen so far.

19
00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.625
A few updates on stories we've covered.

20
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:18.627
Update on the church attack in Jordan: the State Department spokesperson condemned the attack on a funeral service at Saint George's Greek Orthodox Church in Karak.

21
00:02:18.627 --> 00:02:31.600
Update on the West Bank: Reuters reports Israeli forces demolished homes and damaged roads in Hebron, forcing around twelve hundred Palestinians to leave their homes, a day after the attack that killed two Israeli soldiers.

22
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:39.785
And in Vanuatu, Reuters reports another earthquake, magnitude six point one six, according to Germany's GFZ research center.

23
00:02:39.785 --> 00:02:41.993
Now a few quick notes by region.

24
00:02:41.993 --> 00:02:50.986
In Africa, Sahara Reporters reports a local council imposed a night curfew in Ozoro, in Nigeria's Delta State, after cult clashes.

25
00:02:50.986 --> 00:02:57.452
In Latin America, InSight Crime reports Haiti's elections have been postponed again, with no new date set.

26
00:02:57.452 --> 00:03:06.817
In Europe, the Institute for the Study of War reports Ukrainian officials confirmed that Starlink and Starshield satellite service was fully restored in Ukraine yesterday.

27
00:03:06.817 --> 00:03:13.176
And Radio Free Europe reports Serbia is holding a snap election today, amid student led demonstrations.

28
00:03:13.176 --> 00:03:22.064
On cyber, the US Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency, CISA, updated its alert on the PHP Two Shell vulnerability.

29
00:03:22.064 --> 00:03:32.343
It says organizations that can't update right away, or that run PHP version eight point one or earlier, should take affected PHP based systems offline until they are patched.

30
00:03:32.343 --> 00:03:33.751
That's today's brief.

31
00:03:33.751 --> 00:03:41.934
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

32
00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:50.119
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

33
00:03:50.119 --> 00:03:52.243
This brief is digitally narrated.

34
00:03:52.243 --> 00:03:53.181
Questions?

35
00:03:53.181 --> 00:03:56.632
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

36
00:03:56.632 --> 00:03:58.657
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
